BmE Teacher Resources — licensing
=================================

Biology Meets Engineering, University of Cincinnati.
Supported by NSF ITEST grants DRL 1759150 and DRL 2342578.


1. The teaching materials
-------------------------

The lesson plans, prose, tables, diagrams and photographs authored by the
project are licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
    (CC BY-NC 4.0)

Summary:      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
Full terms:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

You are free to share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes,
provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if
changes were made.

Suggested attribution:

    "Biology Meets Engineering teacher materials, University of Cincinnati.
    Supported by NSF ITEST DRL 1759150 and DRL 2342578. Used under CC BY-NC 4.0."

If you are unsure whether your intended use counts as non-commercial — a paid
teacher-training workshop, a fee-charging summer programme, a private school —
please just ask. The intent of this licence is to keep the materials free for
teachers, not to obstruct education. Contact details are in the document.


